## 2. Restrictions
* **No Direct Monetization:** You may not sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or 
  directly charge a fee for access to this Software, its templates, or 
  modified variations of it.
* **No Profit-Making Distribution:** Distribution of this Software, or 
  works derived from it, must be entirely non-profit. You may charge a fee 
  solely to cover the actual, baseline hardware or bandwidth costs of 
  distributing the files (cost-recovery), but you may not generate revenue 
  or profit from its distribution.

## 3. Commercial Infrastructure Exception
For the sake of clarity, commercial entities (such as game server providers 
and hosting companies) ARE permitted to use this Software internally to 
deploy, configure, and manage their server nodes, even if those nodes serve 
paying customers. The commercial ban applies strictly to the monetization, 
sale, or closed-sublicensing of the Software code and templates themselves.

